    "body": "> Please try running [this rust project](https://github.com/davidkna/git-open-repo)\r\n\r\nOutput\r\n```\r\nRepo: \"/Volumes/Files/Dev/test_repo\"\r\nErr(\r\n    NotARepository(\r\n        GitFile(\r\n            Io(\r\n                Custom {\r\n                    kind: Other,\r\n                    error: \"Refusing to open files larger than 65536 bytes, '/Volumes/Files/Dev/test_repo/.git' was 131072 bytes large\",\r\n                },\r\n            ),\r\n        ),\r\n    ),\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere is the output when passed the exact same repo copied to the home directory on the system drive:\r\n```\r\nRepo: \"/Users/me/test_repo\"\r\nOk(\r\n    Repository {\r\n        kind: WorkTree {\r\n            is_linked: false,\r\n        },\r\n        git_dir: \"/Users/me/test_repo/.git\",\r\n        work_dir: Some(\r\n            \"/Users/me/test_repo\",\r\n        ),\r\n    },\r\n)\r\n```\r\n",
